for loop. In contrast to the previous traversal of the container that used the [] operator and
an integer index, this time it is done using an iterator that i) is initialized with begin(), ii) is
moved to the next object in the container via the postfix ++ operator and iii) terminates the
loop when it reaches the object at the slot immediately before the end() iterator. Finally,
the clear method from Section 10.2 is called and the values of size and capacity are
checked again to see its e ff ect.
