CMS :: getFreqEst ( string key ){
minSoFar = numeric limits < >:: max ();
thisCount = 0;
( i = 0; i < D ; i ++) {
thisCount = B [ i ][ fnvHash (i , key )];
( thisCount < minSoFar ) minSoFar = thisCount ;
}
minSoFar ;
}
The for loop computes the value of (10.1). The only problem is obtaining a value for
the estimator that can initialize the search for the minimizer. This is provided by the
numeric limits template class function max with template parameter unsigned long that
returns the largest unsigned long integer that can be represented on the machine.
