This method takes an ifstream object as its argument that corresponds to an input file; for
our specific application the file of interest will be newWords.txt that was created previously
in R from the British National Corpus word data. Data from the file will be read until the
end of the file is encountered: i.e., inFile.eof() evaluates to true. Each word is read in
using the getline function from Section 3.8.5. The resulting key is then “inserted” into the
B array with the insertKey method. To emulate what might transpire while reading from
an actual stream, code has also been included to monitor the frequency of the word “the”
and report on its estimated and actual frequency after every 100,000 words are read from
the “stream”.
